A||N||9||Zorba||V8 head problem||||1||
Z||000000||Zorba||11-08-2000||06:59 PM||||After all the work of installing the engine and doing the convesion, I fire it up - thanks archie for the wiring instructions - <BR>and after about 1 minute I thought I was in heaven! yes...my garage was fill with a white could of white smoke!<BR>Yeah! Damn!<BR>Either my perfomer rpm manifold did not seal tight, or I have warped heads or both. Both head gaskets have been replaced. Torque sequence and all. <BR>Just my luck. Now...solution:<P>1. take the heads to a machine shop<BR>2. Buy a new, more hp heads<BR>3. Buy another engine altogether since this is a 307!<P>Pulling the whole thing out again or most of it and back to square one! Isn't this fun???<BR>I am VERY tempted to just go out and buy me a brand new crate motor under warranty!<P>Has anyone had this bad luck???<P>Zorba||||reg||1
Z||000001||V8Fiero||11-08-2000||07:47 PM||||One question....<P>Did you do any kind of painting to any part of the engine or exhaust? Just wondering, I had painted my exhaust manifolds with heat paint and they smoked something awful till they cured. Just trying to see if it was something simple. Hate to see you go through all that work and have problems.<P>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000002||Terrybogin||11-08-2000||07:52 PM||||A 307???? That is worse than a 305! Toss that thing and get a 350. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||11-08-2000||08:35 PM||||Hehe, Terry! A 307 is purely a "smog" motor, but it's still a small block Chevy and has more power than the 2.8 for sure. However, I much prefer the ol' 350, if I had a choice.<P>Z, lots of reasons it could be smoking. Is the white smoke coming from the exhaust? You sure it's not burning up wires laying against the exhaust or something? Do you see water in the oil (dipstick) or oil floating in the radiator?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Archie||11-08-2000||09:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Zorba:<BR><B>...my garage was fill with a white could of white smoke!<BR>Yeah! Damn!<P>Zorba</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That kind of stuff is why I don't buy used engines for my swaps.<P>Archie<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Zorba||11-09-2000||01:08 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by V8Fiero:<BR><B>One question....<P>Did you do any kind of painting to any part of the engine or exhaust </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Hi Scott. Thanks for the words of concern.<BR>I did paint the block etc but the smoke I am talking about is dense and LOTS of it coming out from both exhaust manifolds/ram horns.<BR>No exhaust system in place yet. Water is getting past the seals or thru a crack on the block. It's pretty bad. Unfortunately, I have to drop the cradle, and now either fix the problem or get a new engine. I need a v8 which will pass emissions as a carburated one. So I am start to shop for a new engine.<BR>Fixing the heads might solve the problem but like someone has stated here, a 307-305 aren't that great for all the work involved in swap. I may just order a crate motor  from a GM dealer. Not sure yet. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Zorba||11-09-2000||01:17 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B> That kind of stuff is why I don't buy used engines for my swaps.<P>Archie<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I must agree. Used engines and many times rebuilt ones can hide problems that even the rebuilder may not be aware of. There was a guy here in town selling a souped up motor with some 400+ hp (desktop dyno) for $2,000<BR>completed carb to pan. But the thing was never fired or tested in any way. So, you don't know if all internal clearances and specs are "exact" and you don't know what you are buying until you fire it up. <P>Of course, if you fire it up and something goes screwy, the guy who sells you the engine won't warranty a damn thing. I know GM has a couple of budget engines pushing about 300hp and they come with a warranty. <P>Since I already have all the peripherals - carb, wires, manifolds, distributor, etc, a NEW crate motor at least should give me some sort of peace of mind so that this "sh*&gt;* won't happen again.<P>I went thru a lot of work to put this together (by myself in my garage)and then, when it's all done, bang, it smokes like a hay stack. <P>As I understand it, most crate engines are tested at the factory prior to being sold. Or I hope they are. This is my ONLY and last conversion so I want it to last and be enjoyable in the future.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Indiana_resto_guy||11-09-2000||07:36 AM||||Zorba,<P>Is all you let it run was for 1 minute?<BR>I've done lots of stuff with small block chevys, and found if the engine has sat around for a while they do tend to smoke LOTS on initial start-up. If it runs steady and doesn't stumble, run it at fast idle for a while and see what happens nest time you start. That particular problem has happened when I've had the heads off, don't give up yet!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Zorba||11-09-2000||09:58 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Indiana_resto_guy:<BR><B>Zorba,<P>Is all you let it run was for 1 minute?<BR>I've done lots of stuff with small !</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Now I let it idle for about 3-4 minutes at a time...this WAS a marine engine. I am being told that maybe the heads are warped but I have not had them checked. I am running a performer rpm manifold which fits perfect. Correct gaskets etc. I just ran into some bad luck here somewhere in the process. Since I am not a mechanic, the heads and manifold were installed by an engineer who has had years of experience rebuilding small block chevys. This was his motor. The torque sequence was followed by the book - I was there - the heads examined.etc.<BR>Maybe I should have my head examined before I buy my next motor. <BR>||||reg||6
Z||000009||Zorba||11-12-2000||11:28 PM|||| No more problems. Went out and bought a h.o. 350 engine. Going thru the install process. No more crappy 305-307 used piece of garbage. Thanks for your input.||||reg||1
